Description: Quit cleanly when the desktop session ends, as the Inhibit portal reports it.
 A desktop session tells its applications through the session monitor of the Inhibit portal that it ends, while it
 still runs. GTK 4 applications and Chromium quit then. Firefox did not create such a monitor, so it ran until systemd
 stopped it with SIGTERM, at the same time as the compositor, and GTK ends a process whose Wayland connection breaks.
 .
 nsNativeAppSupportUnix, which follows an X11 session through XSMP, now creates a session monitor when it is enabled,
 except in background task mode. It answers the query whether the session may end at once, and when the session ends,
 quits with nsIAppStartup::Quit(eForceQuit), as the XSMP "die" callback does. A monitor ends with the portal process,
 so a new one is created whenever another process owns the portal's name, and the calls do not start the portal, which
 stops at the end of the session. AsyncDBus.h gains GetPortalSessionPath(), which names the session of the monitor.
Author: Mitar
Bug: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2090663
Forwarded: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340640
Last-Update: 2026-11-11
